\name{cellucid_field_categories}
\alias{cellucid_field_categories}
\title{Read the categories of a field}
\usage{
cellucid_field_categories(viewer, field)
}
\arguments{
\item{viewer}{A viewer \code{\link{cellucid_view}()} or \code{\link{cellucid_serve}()} returned.}
\item{field}{A field by name: source "obs" for a column of the cells, "var" for a gene; key is the name as shown. A named list. Required. \describe{\item{\code{key}}{The field or gene name as the app shows it. Text (at least 1 character). Required.}\item{\code{source}}{"obs" for a column of the cells, "var" for a gene. One of \code{"obs"}, \code{"var"}. Required.}}}
}
\value{
A \code{cellucid_action_request}, at once and invisibly: the action is sent now, or when the viewer's channel opens.
\code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} returns what it read: a list of \code{categories}, \code{field}, \code{missing} (Open cells without a category), \code{view} (The view the colors and shown counts are of (the selected one), named as actions name views ("View N")). Cells in it are original positions (0-based rows of the dataset's obs).
}
\description{
Each category of a categorical field with its cells, the cells shown in the active view, its color and whether it is shown.
}
\details{
The viewer's action \code{field.categories} (Dataset). It reads, and changes nothing: it makes no step of the history.
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{cellucid_act}()} sends any action by its type, and \code{\link{cellucid_action_result}()}
